# AGENTS.md — `reporting/`

Root [`../AGENTS.md`](../AGENTS.md) applies. Reporting source and interpretation
are human-owned; agents assist and hand drafts back for review.

## Allowed assistance

- Draft/revise prose explicitly for human review, based on real project evidence.
- Wire data-derived figures from `../results/figures/` and authored schematics
  from `../assets/figures/`.
- Build artifacts, fix source/build errors, and maintain shared references/style.
- Validate an existing delivery without changing it.

## Human gates

- Do not finalize, commit as accepted, submit, or otherwise represent scientific
  prose as human-approved without the user.
- Do not fabricate or interpolate results, numbers, citations, interpretations,
  registered-run IDs, figure provenance, or delivery metadata.
- Creating a delivery freezes a point-in-time external artifact and is a durable
  mutation. Run the delivery command only with explicit user approval.
- Do not edit a delivery in place. A change requires a new dated milestone.

## Source and delivery rules

- While drafting, reference canonical generated/authored figure sources rather
  than maintaining copies. Copying exact payloads and figures is required only
  inside an immutable delivery.
- A delivery must use a human-approved registered provenance archive, not merely
  whatever happens to be in current `results/provenance.json`.
- Keep text and files up to 1 MiB in Git. Larger delivery binaries use
  {{ data_versioning }} at the same logical path; commit the pointer and
  `delivery.yaml`.
- Never edit generated `_assets/theme-colors*.tex`; change `conf/theme/` and
  rebuild.
- Preserve legacy `submissions/` snapshots. Do not rename or migrate user
  history automatically.
